# AGENTS.md — {{APP_NAME}} recordings

This folder holds {{APP_NAME}}'s recorded scenarios: Playwright flows that run as
end-to-end tests or are recorded into demo videos with Runcast. For
AI assistants that write or fix scenarios here.

Read before working:

1. [`PROJECT.md`](PROJECT.md): the app's screens and records, known forms,
   selectors, known behaviours, and the catalogs of helpers and steps.
2. The kit's skills: from the Runcast plugin (Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity),
   and also in `.kit/skills/` (the runtime link, present after setup):
   - [`runcast-setup`](.kit/skills/runcast-setup/SKILL.md): onboarding a
     project; keeping `PROJECT.md` and the login flow up to date.
   - [`runcast-plan`](.kit/skills/runcast-plan/SKILL.md):
     plan a new scenario with the user, question by question, into
     `scenarios/<name>.md`.
   - [`runcast-scenario`](.kit/skills/runcast-scenario/SKILL.md): turn the
     text into `scenarios/<name>.spec.ts`; the rules for steps and helpers.
   - [`runcast-publish`](.kit/skills/runcast-publish/SKILL.md): upload a
     rendered video to YouTube.
3. The kit's guide: [`.kit/README.md`](.kit/README.md).

Commands: `node {{DIR}}/.kit/cli.ts <command>` from the repository root
(`setup`, `doctor`, `test`, `rehearsal`, `video`, `render`, `narration`,
`youtube`). If `.kit` is missing, run the plugin's `setup` again (see the
runcast-setup skill).

Most important rules:

- Three layers: scenarios (`scenarios/*.spec.ts`) only order **steps**; steps
  (`steps/`) are reusable and check their result; helpers (`helpers/`) do the
  screen work. Missing ones are added there and listed in `PROJECT.md`.
- Every click, drag and hover goes through `rec` (`rec.click`, `rec.drag`...),
  never `page.click`: otherwise the cursor and the camera miss it.
- Steps never call `rec.step`; `scenario()` marks them and the step's `note` is
  its on-screen message. Nothing is drawn in the page.
- Project code imports the kit (and Playwright types) only through `kit.ts`.
- A new scenario is first written as text with the user (`scenarios/<name>.md`)
  and only then as a test; both stay in sync.
- Values come from `.env.local` and are listed in `.env.example`. Passwords
  never reach code, logs or chats (`rec.typeSecret`).
- Every scenario passes in all modes (`test`, `rehearsal`, `video`).
  `rec.pause` is for the viewer only.
- Ask the user about voice-over, captions, title cards and blurred fields when
  planning a video (plan skill, phase 1).
- Scenarios write to a real backend: ask before running them.
- The kit is shared and app-agnostic: never edit files under `.kit`; changes
  belong in the Runcast repository.
